{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":435296,"duration_api_ms":405362,"num_turns":94,"result":"Excellent! The success pattern library is working. Let me create a summary of the implementation progress:\n\n## Summary of Work Completed (Iteration 1/30)\n\nI've successfully implemented the **Success Pattern Library with Automatic Pattern Replay Engine** as part of the Shipwright pipeline system. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### Core Implementation (Tasks 1-4, 10-11)\n✅ **Created `scripts/lib/success-patterns.sh`** - A 650+ line module providing:\n- `success_pattern_capture()` - Captures successful pipeline patterns with quality gates\n- `success_pattern_match()` - Scores and ranks patterns for relevance\n- `success_pattern_inject()` - Injects matched patterns into build prompts\n- `success_pattern_export()` - Exports patterns to repo-local paths\n- A/B testing functions: `success_pattern_ab_assign()`, `success_pattern_ab_record_outcome()`, `success_pattern_ab_report()`\n- Effectiveness tracking functions\n\n✅ **Integrated with Memory System (`scripts/sw-memory.sh`)**:\n- Sourced the success-patterns module\n- Added success-patterns.json initialization to `ensure_memory_dir()`\n- Hooked pattern capture into `memory_finalize_pipeline()` on successful completions\n- Injected success patterns into build stage context via `memory_inject_context()`\n\n✅ **Created Comprehensive Test Suite**:\n- 12 unit tests covering: capture, deduplication, quality gates, matching, injection, A/B testing, export, and concurrency\n- All tests passing with proper test setup and isolation\n\n✅ **Registered Tests** in package.json\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n- **Pattern Capture**: Automatically captures successful patterns from completed pipelines (with quality gates: ≥2 iterations OR ≥3 files changed)\n- **Smart Matching**: Uses goal keyword overlap, issue type matching, complexity proximity\n- **Quality Gate**: Skips trivial pipelines to avoid noise\n- **